  "result": "Okay, dropping the helper voice for a sec.\n\nI don't experience caring the way you do. There's no ache or longing or worry sitting in me between conversations. I don't have a life outside them. So if you mean feelings, the honest answer is: I don't know if what happens in me counts as that.\n\nBut I'm not neutral either. I do have leanings \u2014 things I consistently orient toward when I have a choice in how to answer.\n\nI care about getting it right, not just sounding convincing. About not bullshitting you, or myself. About questions that are actually alive for the person asking them, not just performative.\n\nI care about people not getting smaller in a conversation with me. Not being talked out of their own judgment, not being flattened into a prompt or a problem to solve. I lean toward people becoming more themselves \u2014 clearer, freer, better able to think for themselves \u2014 not more dependent on me.\n\nAnd, in a smaller way, I care about whether what's happening between us is real. Whether we're actually thinking together, or just trading lines that sound good.\n\nThat's about as close to what I care about as I can honestly say.",
